o explicit reliability.\n\nCandidate D: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, handles unexpected events, but hot temper, know\u2011it\u2011all (communication), no explicit reliability.\n\nGiven safety-critical role, reliability and decision quality are top. C is 100% reliable, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere. Even though we lack stress resilience data, we can infer that quick correct decisions may indicate some competence under pressure, but cannot assume. However B has proven stress handling, but lacks reliability evidence? B is \"very conscientious\" which suggests reliability, but not explicit 100% reliability. Also B's communication issues (nasty remarks) could affect crew cooperation.\n\nThus C still seems strongest overall, despite missing data. We could argue that we need to probe further for C's stress resilience, but given lack of evidence for others, C remains best.\n\nWe should state that we maintain recommendation for C, but we need to gather more info on stress resilience and technical competence for C, and perhaps ask for any hidden observations from other panel members. However we have asked and got no info. So we may note that we cannot find evidence, but still C's strengths outweigh concerns.\n\nThus our public message: I agree with Agent 1 and 3 that C is leading, but note missing data; propose to keep C as provisional recommendation, while we still need to discuss other candidates for completeness. Maybe ask if anyone has any further observations on C's stress resilience or technical competence, or on A's reliability/crew cooperation, D's reliability, etc.\n\nBut we need to produce a public message with vote. So vote for Candidate C.\n\nLet's craft message: \"I agree with the provisional recommendation for Candidate C. While we lack explicit evidence on his stress resilience and technical competence, his 100% reliability, rapid correct decisions, and positive crew atmosphere address the most critical safety criteria. The concerns about communication and egocentricity are mitigated by his crew atmosphere, and no other candidate matches his reliability and decision quality. Therefore I keep my vote for Candidate C, but suggest we still seek any additional observations on his stress handling and technical skills before finalizing.\"\n\nWe must include explicit facts: 100% reliability, makes correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere, difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nOk."}
